  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Strategic Imaginations (2020), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 1 time. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 2,144 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Strategic Imaginations by Anke Gilleir and Aude Defurne was published by Leuven University Press in 2020. Conceptually, the work connects to Presidency, Power (physics), Democracy, Politics and German.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 1 citation. Notable citing venues include Public humanities.. The citing authors are based in the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 2,144 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Reduced inequalities among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\" data-wiki-books=\"verified\">The latest English Wikipedia check verified 2 article–work reference matches. These are references or bibliography entries, which may include other editions of the same work; they do not measure readership.</p>\n",
